.TH RS485EMULATORAPI 3 "September 2026" "wRS485_emulator" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
RS485emulatorAPI - API for accessing the wRS485_emulator virtual RS485 ports

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <RS485emulatorAPI.h>

.BI "wError_t init_RS485emulatorAPI(void);"

.BI "void close_RS485emulatorAPI(void);"

.BI "wError_t release_RS485emulatorAPI(const char *" serialport ");"

.BI "wError_t takePort_RS485emulatorAPI(char *" port ");"

.BI "wError_t getMPort_RS485emulatorAPI(char *" fpname ");"
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION
The 
.B RS485emulatorAPI
interface provides functions used by (sever and master) applications to access and manage virtual serial ports exported by
.BR wRS485_emulator.
When the process starts, it provides a virtual master-port and a set of virtual slave-port. All necessary data to get one of
them, is managed by a SQLite3 file-database, where the file location is defined by the 
.BR RS485_PORTSDBFILE.

First of all, your process needs to open a channel to the DB. You can achieve the result calling the
.BR init_RS485emulatorAPI ()
function. It must be executed before using any other API functions.

When the obtained virtual serial port is no longer required,
.BR close_RS485emulatorAPI ()
should be called to release the system resorces and close the channel to database.

.SH FUNCTIONS

.TP
.B init_RS485emulatorAPI()
It initializes the APIs and returns one of the following exit-code:
.nf
RS485EMULE_SUCCESS         // The module has been correctly initialized
RS485EMULE_ERROR_IOFAILED  // Database read/write operation failed
.fi

.TP
.B "close_RS485emulatorAPI()"
It closes the database channel used by the RS485 emulator API. No error code is returned.

.TP
.BI "release_RS485emulatorAPI(const char *" serialport ")"
It marks the argument defined virtual-port as an available one. It allows another process to use it.
You have to close the open port's file-descriptor begore to use this API. This function returns one of the following values:
.nf
RS485EMULE_SUCCESS                OK, the porst is available now
RS485EMULE_WARNING_NOTHINGTODO    The port was already available
RS485EMULE_ERROR_ITEMNOTFOUND     The required port does not exists
RS485EMULE_ERROR_INTERNAL         Database table has been created in a wrong way
RS485EMULE_ERROR_FORBIDDENOP      The port is in use by another proc
RS485EMULE_WARNING_TIMEOUT
.fi

.TP
.BI "takePort_RS485emulatorAPI(char *" port ")"
This function allows you to acquire an available virtual slave serial port.
Retured values:
.nf
RS485EMULE_SUCCESS               The port has been reserved
RS485EMULE_ERROR_ITEMNOTFOUND    No available ports
RS485EMULE_ERROR_FORBIDDENOP     You attemt to write into a read-only DB
RS485EMULE_ERROR_UNKNOWN         Unknown error
RS485EMULE_WARNING_TIMEOUT       Reached timeout. But the function could be re-executed with success
RS485EMULE_ERROR_UNAVAILRES      The function failed, the resource was unexpectly unavailable
.fi

.TP
.BI "getMPort_RS485emulatorAPI(char *" fpname ")"
This function is used by the process with master role to get the the serial port name it has to use.
If the name is an empty string then it means the RS485 emulator has not yet created the virtual port
Retured values:
.nf
RS485EMULE_SUCCESS                The master port has been correctly assigned to the process
RS485EMULE_WARNING_NOTHINGTODO    The port is already assigned to the process
RS485EMULE_WARNING_TIMEOUT        The database is temporary unavailable
RS485EMULE_ERROR_INTERNAL         Unknown (and unexpected) error
RS485EMULE_ERROR_ITEMNOTFOUND     No port available
RS485EMULE_ERROR_EXTTOOLFAILURE   rs485_updateTool returned an error
.fi

.SH RETURN VALUE
In order to reports the SQLite error messages, almost all the functions return a (type =
.BR WERROR_WITHMESSAGE
)
.BI wError
object as ertor code. In this way the error will reports the SQLite3 text message asfter the main error-code defined by the
symbols in the
.BR RS485_errorCodes.h
heade file. It can be veryu useful during debug sessions.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wRS485_emulator (1), wError (3) 

